AUREUS-000 — DOCUMENT 38

CONSTITUTIONAL STEWARDSHIP

Status: Pre-Ratification Draft (Revision Candidate)

---

Purpose

This document establishes how the Constitution of Aureus is stewarded throughout the life of the institution. It defines constitutional authority, accountability, continuity, and the orderly transition from a founder-managed organization to permanent constitutional governance.

The Constitution exists to govern Aureus.

No person, office, or organization exists above it.

---

Section 1 — Constitutional Supremacy

This Constitution is the highest governing document of Aureus.

Every policy, procedure, technological system, partnership, financial decision, and operational practice shall conform to this Constitution.

Where a conflict exists, this Constitution prevails.

No person may disregard a constitutional provision because it is inconvenient, profitable, expedient, or popular.

---

Section 2 — Founding Stewardship

During the Founding Phase, Aureus operates as a founder-managed limited liability company.

The Managing Member of Aureus LLC serves as the Constitutional Steward.

The Constitutional Steward is entrusted with protecting, applying, and preserving this Constitution.

This office exists to steward the Constitution—not to stand above it.

The Constitutional Steward possesses only those authorities granted by this Constitution.

---

Section 3 — Duties of the Constitutional Steward

The Constitutional Steward shall:

- faithfully uphold this Constitution;
- preserve the Mission, Eternal Principles, and Member Rights;
- ensure institutional decisions remain consistent with this Constitution;
- publish constitutional interpretations that materially affect institutional practice;
- maintain transparency regarding constitutional amendments;
- preserve institutional continuity;
- prepare Aureus for permanent constitutional governance.

The Constitutional Steward is accountable to this Constitution in every action.

---

Section 4 — Constitutional Limits

The Constitutional Steward shall not:

- suspend this Constitution;
- ignore constitutional rights;
- diminish the Unamendable Core;
- authorize conduct prohibited by this Constitution;
- conceal constitutional violations;
- claim emergency authority beyond that granted by this Constitution.

No office within Aureus possesses unlimited authority.

---

Section 5 — Constitutional Interpretation

Questions concerning the meaning or application of this Constitution shall receive written constitutional interpretations.

Each interpretation shall:

- identify the constitutional provisions considered;
- explain the reasoning supporting the interpretation;
- preserve the Mission and Eternal Principles;
- become part of the permanent constitutional record.

Interpretations clarify this Constitution.

They do not amend it.

---

Section 6 — Transparency

Constitutional stewardship shall be conducted openly whenever consistent with member privacy, safety, and lawful confidentiality.

Aureus shall maintain a permanent public constitutional record including:

- amendments;
- constitutional interpretations;
- constitutional reviews;
- ratification history;
- superseded provisions;
- annual constitutional stewardship reports.

Transparency strengthens institutional trust.

---

Section 7 — Transition to Permanent Governance

The Founding Phase exists only to establish Aureus as a stable institution.

When Aureus reaches constitutional maturity, stewardship authority shall transition from sole constitutional stewardship to permanent constitutional governance as provided by this Constitution.

The transition shall be deliberate, documented, and publicly announced.

The purpose of transition is not to replace stewardship, but to distribute it responsibly.

---

Section 8 — Constitutional Maturity

Permanent constitutional governance shall be established only after Aureus demonstrates sufficient institutional maturity.

The maturity criteria shall be objective, published, and reviewed before transition.

These criteria shall include institutional capacity, operational stability, stewardship readiness, financial sustainability, and the demonstrated ability to preserve the Constitution across multiple leaders.

No transition shall occur merely because time has passed.

---

Section 9 — Future Council of Stewardship

Upon constitutional maturity, Aureus shall establish a permanent Council of Stewardship in accordance with this Constitution.

The Council shall assume those constitutional responsibilities assigned to it through lawful amendment and ratification.

Its authority exists to preserve this Constitution, not to replace it.

No Council may exercise powers beyond those granted by this Constitution.

---

Section 10 — Enduring Stewardship

Constitutional stewardship is a permanent institutional responsibility.

Leadership may change.

Technology may change.

Organizations may change.

The Constitution endures.

Every generation of Aureus inherits the responsibility to preserve it faithfully for those who come after.

The measure of constitutional stewardship is not institutional power, but institutional faithfulness.

Every constitutional decision shall ultimately answer one question:

"Does this preserve the ability of Aureus to help people flourish—forever?"